s. Therefore, the only consistent interpretation is that the 'minimum outcome' is the lowest value possible in the decision problem: 0 Euros. Only Lottery A can yield 0 (with 1%), B cannot. So P(0 in A) = 1%, P(0 in B) = 0%. The reason prefers the lottery with the higher probability of this minimum outcome — so it would prefer A. But this is a preference for greater risk of zero, which is unusual. Alternatively, the reason might be misworded, and intended to mean 'prefers the lottery with the lower probability of the minimum outcome' (i.e., risk aversion). But we must follow the definition as given. So: the reason prefers A over B because A has a higher chance (1% vs 0%) of the minimum outcome (0 Euros).",
